* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jar binary

# The vendored-modules tree is byte-verbatim BY LAW (NOTICE's own "no
# reformatting, no re-indentation" clause) -- line-ending normalization
# has no business anywhere in it. Found the hard way (vendoring batch
# 3, AR-VB3-R1, notes/adr/0072-vendoring-batch-3.md): the root rule
# above silently normalized `lookup_tables/uti_recurrence.csv` (CRLF
# upstream) to LF on checkout while its NOTICE row kept recording the
# true CRLF hash, so the row stayed honest while a fresh clone got the
# wrong bytes. -text disables normalization entirely, the same fix
# this file already uses for the HL7 ER7 fixtures below.
components/sim/resources/sim/modules/** -text

# HL7v2 ER7 messages use \r (not \n) as their segment separator; these
# demo transcripts carry that wire format literally (blank-line-
# separated messages, \r within each). -text disables line-ending
# normalization so a checkout on any platform can't rewrite those
# bytes -- same hazard and same fix as ehr-testing-tools' own
# .gitattributes for its v2 fixtures.
#
# Relocated (demos front door, AR-DM-1, 2026-08-07): the pattern moves
# in the SAME commit as the files it protects -- moving the files
# without the pattern is exactly the hazard class AR-VB3-R1 closed for
# the vendored-modules tree, above.
demos/traces/**/messages*.txt -text

# The same hazard, for ehr-testing-tools' own v2 fixtures -- carried
# over from tools' pre-carve .gitattributes (H2 landing) but never
# actually added here until the discipline-parity session's own
# fixture relocation (2026-07-28) surfaced the gap: these files sat
# unprotected at their old root test/fixtures/v2/ path since the carve.
components/corpus/test-fixtures/v2/*.hl7 -text
components/corpus/test-fixtures/v2/simhospital/messages.out -text

